{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqqqrlczyc2","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"tested status satisfies blocking deps safely for impl to impl dispatch","summary":"Judge finding (codex/fix-stale-reaper-readiness): changing dep-satisfaction from status==='done' to done OR tested (DEP_SATISFIED_STATUSES, daemon.js depSatisfied at the makeResolver effective gate) is safe even though the daemon spawn selector (decideOne) does not distinguish judge from impl dependents and a fresh attempt forks from the dispatcher-chosen base defaulting to HEAD (routes/subconscious.js createWorktree opts.base||'HEAD'). The impl to impl wrong-base hazard (a dependent forking off main while its prereq is only tested/committed-but-unmerged) is NOT realized because: (a) tested is a transient pre-merge state immediately consumed by the paired judge, which under automode auto-merges on APPROVE, flipping tested to merged within one judge cycle; (b) impl-to-impl code dependencies are deliberately serialized by the dispatcher (parallel-dispatch.md: graph tracks logical deps not file contention; file-coupled tasks dispatched one-at-a-time after the prior completes/merges); (c) under the feature-branch tier the base is the feature branch with tier-1 auto-merge of approved attempts before the next forks off it; (d) dispatch is dispatcher-mediated (prepare with chosen base), not autonomous daemon process-spawn. The only pre-merge consumer of tested is the judge, which reviews the attempt branch directly (no base dependency). Hazard requires a dispatcher to manually wire impl-B blocked_by impl-A and spawn B off default base mid-judge, which the contract explicitly forbids.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T14:30:28.835Z","vec":[-0.12561506032943726,-0.004452338442206383,0.020381461828947067,-0.02292298525571823,0.026513133198022842,-0.10345643758773804,-0.017123254016041756,0.07208788394927979,-0.008634842000901699,0.08649436384439468,0.030152590945363045,0.0064746